    4 | "desc:Hyperreal FAUST Panner (New Renderer)\n\n// #HELP: New FAUST perceptual renderer. Artistic/Physical are approximate cue models, not the original KEMAR renderer.\n// #HELP: Same canvas, automation and manager shell; new smoothed timing, shadow, comb-pinna, six early taps and eight late feedback combs.\n// #HELP: Travel time is bounded to 65534 samples. This renderer deliberately sounds different.\n// #TOOLTIP: New FAUST headphone panner; original controls with a new audio model.\n\noptions:gfx_hz=60\noptions:idle=always\noptions:ownership=auto\n\nin_pin:left input\nin_pin:right input\nout_pin:left output\nout_pin:right output\n\n// Retired parameter slots. Keep indices and types for saved-state/automation compatibility.\n// These parameters are hidden and have no effect.\nslider1:#retired_text_1=\"\"<string>-Retired 1\nslider2:#retired_text_2=\"\"<string>-Retired 2\nslider3:1<1,999,1>-Retired 3\nslider4:0<0,1,1{Unused,Unused}>-Retired 4\nslider5:1<0,1,0.001>-Retired 5\n\n// POSITION\n// #TOOLTIP: Left/right object placement. Negative = left, positive = right.\nslider6:0<-1,1,0.001>-Lateral\n// #TOOLTIP: Physical distance throw. V6 uses a shorter, higher-resolution stage range than V5.\nslider7:0.25<0,1,0.001>-Distance\n// #TOOLTIP: Front/rear object placement. +1 = front wall, 0 = side plane, -1 = rear wall.\nslider8:0.82<-1,1,0.001>-Depth Front/Rear\n\n// FEEL\n// #TOOLTIP: Directional cue intensity. Higher emphasizes timing and spectral placement cues.\nslider9:0.58<0,1,0.001>-Spatial Throw\n// #TOOLTIP: Apparent source size. Lower = tighter point source; higher = wider / more diffuse image.\nslider10:0.10<0,1,0.001>-Size\n// #TOOLTIP: Out-of-head realism cue strength. Formerly Externalize.\nslider11:0.42<0,1,0.001>-Push Out\n// #TOOLTIP: Early reflection amount. Higher = more room cue and more externalization, less surgical precision.\nslider12:0.30<0,1,0.001>-Room\n\n// MATERIAL / MOTION\n// #TOOLTIP: How blocked or hidden the source is. Higher = more muffled direct sound and more reflection dominance.\nslider13:0<0,1,0.001>-Occlusion\n// #TOOLTIP: Tiny motion added to keep static sources from collapsing inward on headphones.\nslider14:0.04<0,1,0.001>-Micro Motion\n// #TOOLTIP: Final output trim after spatial processing.\nslider15:0<-18,12,0.1>-Output Trim (dB)\n\n// AUTOMATION / ADVANCED\n// #TOOLTIP: Caps aggressive spatial throw and uses safer smoothing for automation curves.\nslider16:1<0,1,1>-Automation Safe\n// #TOOLTIP: Perceptual compression curve. Higher values make moderate visual angles less extreme.\nslider17:2.00<1,3,0.01>-Cue Curve\n// #TOOLTIP: Movement smoothing in milliseconds. Automation Safe enforces a higher minimum.\nslider18:90<5,250,1>-Motion Smooth (ms)\n// #TOOLTIP: Geometric room scale for the bounce model. Higher = larger room and longer early reflection timing.\nslider19:0.55<0,1,0.001>-Room Size\n// Retired parameter slot; hidden and inert.\nslider20:1<1,64,1>-Retired 20\n// #TOOLTIP: Artistic height cues, or Physical elevation from -90 to +90 degrees. Perceived localization depends on the listener and source bandwidth.\nslider21:0<-1,1,0.001>-Elevation\n// #TOOLTIP: Input interpretation. Mono Emitter folds to mono; Stereo/Dual preserve source width; Ambience Bed preserves field material instead of forcing a point source.\nslider22:0<0,3,1{Mono,Stereo,Bed,Dual}>-Source Mode\n// #TOOLTIP: How much original stereo side/difference content survives in Stereo/Dual/Ambience modes. Leave high for beds/music; lower for point sources.\nslider23:0.75<0,1,0.001>-Input Width Preserve\n// #TOOLTIP: Ambience Bed only. Lower = broad stable bed; higher = more world-locked bed biased by object placement.\nslider24:0.45<0,1,0.001>-Bed Anchor\n// #TOOLTIP: UI-only canvas drag limiter. Default +-10 deg makes POV placement quick; Quick Controls and snap chips still allow full-range placement.\nslider25:10<0,90,0.1>-POV Canvas Range (deg)\n\n// SCENEVERB LITE / OPTIONAL LATE FIELD\n// Hard compatibility